  "description": "ODOHAT crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H134 Gd16 N24 O61 12+,3(C8 H20 N1 1+),15(Cl1 1-),H2 O1,C2 H6 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd10 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd11 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd12 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd13 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd14 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd15 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd16 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 33 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.538-4.143 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.38-117.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C90 H134 Gd16 N24 O61 12+,3(C8 H20 N1 1+),15(Cl1 1-),H2 O1,C2 H6 O1.",
